## Data Source

Endings and articles (the rules) are static:
- `@/constants/agreement` (AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS) — 15 paradigms
- `GENDER_MOVES` and `NOUN_NOTES` are local to `components/nouns-section.tsx`; the
  card rows are derived from AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS. There is no `@/constants/nouns`.

Example words and per-pattern counts are **loaded from the database** by
`loadNouns` in `routes/reference/$tab.tsx`, grouped by `groupNounsByPattern`
(`@/lib/noun-paradigm-groups`). Nouns fall back to each paradigm's static
`example` when a pattern has no corpus members.

## Verification

- [x] greek-first: Greek forms prominent in all paradigms
- [x] paradigm-tables: Case (rows) x pattern (columns), singular and plural as row groups under one header
- [x] progressive-disclosure: only "Every pattern in the course" is collapsible
- [x] function-first-labels: Doer / Target / Owner lead, grammar terms as sublabels
- [x] frequency-priority: per-pattern counts come from the corpus, not a static label
- [x] no-redundancy: each gender is named once per view (a chip spans same-gender columns); cells are neutral
- [x] colour-honesty: gender colour on the gender cards, case colour only on the lookup's row headers
- [x] rules-tested: every rule the page states is checked against AGREEMENT_PARADIGMS in agreement.test.ts
- [x] contextual-examples: example words are real corpus nouns, ordered by CEFR then frequency
